title: Frecent folders
tags: [[Panel types]]
kind: reference
aliases: folder-open zoxide frecency
summary: Jumping to a folder you use often and lately, zoxide-style — opened in the file manager, or listed (its children or its whole subtree) in the metarecord list.

`folder:open` is a pick of the command input, like `recent` ([[recent panel]]): it
offers the folders of the metarecords you viewed in this repository, the most
''frecent'' first — frequently and recently used — each with its score, and opens the
one you pick. Type to narrow; the filter is the command input's ordered substring
match, so `mu ja` finds `/music/jazz`. A bare folder path typed inline is a pick too.

|!Key |!Opens the folder |
|<<key "folder:open files here" "g d">> |in the [[file-manager panel]] |
|<<key "folder:open children here" "g c">> |in the [[metarecord-list panel]], as `mfr_path -> "<folder>"`: its direct children |
|<<key "folder:open subtree here" "g t">> |in the [[metarecord-list panel]], as `mfr_path ->* "<folder>"`: everything under it ([[Following references]]) |

Here by default, as `cd` would; the `i`, `w` and `b` prefixes choose here, the other
slot or a new workspace ([[Panel slots and layout]]). The command is
`folder:open <view> <where> <folder>`, with `files`, `children` or `subtree` as the
view.

!! Which folders, in which order

The candidates come from the recently-viewed list, where each metarecord carries a
''rank'': one per view ([[Why recently viewed is kept by the GUI]]). Two things count
as a view of a folder:

* going into it in the [[file-manager panel]] — once per arrival, not again when the same folder is listed anew (a refresh, an operation);
* viewing anything ''in'' it: a file the [[file panel]] or `metarecord-detail` shows counts for its parent folder.

A folder is worth the sum of its entries, each entry its rank weighted by how long ago
it was last viewed — zoxide's weights:

|!Last viewed |!Weight |
|less than an hour ago |×4 |
|less than a day ago |×2 |
|less than a week ago |×½ |
|older |×¼ |

The same score orders the [[recent panel]] and the `recent` pick when asked to, entry by
entry. The weights are those of `frecency` in the shared panel helpers
(`panel-shim/ui.js`, served as `/__ui.js`), so the panel and the picks cannot disagree;
the folders are gathered by `frecentFolders` in the shipped `gui/commands.js`
([[User commands]]). A record without a position in the tree — an orphan, a record with
no file — counts for nothing, and neither does a folder that has lost its own.

Because an entry is a metarecord and not a path, a folder keeps its history when it
is renamed or moved, which zoxide cannot do.

!! How the ranks age

As in zoxide, the ranks do not grow forever: once they add up to more than 1000, every
rank is multiplied by 0.9 and the entries left under one go. The 200 most recently
viewed are always kept, whatever their rank, so a burst of new views never empties
the list; beyond them stays only what was viewed often. `crates/gui/src/recent.rs`
holds the constants.
